5. CERT Polska (CSIRT NASK) Dangerous Websites Warning List (bundled
   malicious-host list)
   The data comes from CERT Polska. Source: https://cert.pl/lista-ostrzezen/
   Feed: https://hole.cert.pl/domains/v2/domains.txt
   The list publishes no licence text. On 2026-09-01 EdgeXene LLC asked
   CERT Polska in writing whether commercial software may use the list for
   phishing and malicious-domain protection, process or convert it into
   another technical format, and redistribute an updated copy of the
   resulting list to its users, with attribution to CERT Polska / NASK and
   without representing the data as its own or selling the list. On
   2026-09-11 CSIRT NASK / CERT Polska replied that "All the conditions
   described are certainly sufficient for implementation" and asked, in
   addition to stating that the data comes from CERT Polska, for a link to
   https://cert.pl/lista-ostrzezen/. Both requests are met here, on the
   About page at patanyx.net, and in the header of every list published
   through the signed update channel.
   The CERT Polska entries travel ONLY in that signed update channel, as the
   request to CERT Polska described. They are not in the committed
   crates/app/src/blocklist.txt, so they are not compiled into releases and
   are not published in this repository; scripts/test-certpl.sh refuses a
   tree whose committed list contains them. Where they do appear they are
   included by CERT Polska's permission and are not licensed under the
   Apache 2.0 licence that covers this repository.
   (Wired in 2026-09-11 behind BLOCKLIST_ENABLE_CERTPL, which the publisher
   enables in its own environment and which stays off in this tree.)

